 ],
 "why": "The statement asks only that mu(1/2)=0 for zeta. Exponent improvements (1908-2017) are bounds, all pre-snapshot; journal publication treated as digestion. Constant-only improvements (Hiary-Patel-Yang, Revers) leave mu(1/2) unchanged, so none. Claimed full proofs (Kuznetsov, Chaudhry, Cheng et al., Unterberger) are not_credible on several F10 signals, Aizenberg withdrawn. Analogues (other series, zero ordinates, Barnes zeta, general sequences, Bohr's problem) and zero-proportion / zero-free-region results are variants; their AI generation is recorded per event but does not touch this problem. Furmaniak's Claude disclosure doesn't say what the model produced, so none (and the event is a variant anyway). Post-snapshot reformulations and heuristics are none.",
 "doubts": "Bourgain's exponent 13/84 vs 53/342 unresolved; irrelevant to status. Pre-2024 bound events rest on the Wikipedia table only.",
